          "title": "Recursion and the DP Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Recursion",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Recursion = ==base case== + **recursive case** that shrinks the problem",
                "{red:Missing or unreachable base case} → stack overflow",
                "Each call gets its own ==stack frame==; depth n costs **O(n)** space",
                "Python's default limit is ~==1000 frames==, then `RecursionError`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. When DP Applies",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Overlapping subproblems==: the same state is needed again and again",
                "==Optimal substructure==: the best answer is built from best sub-answers",
                "Both must hold, otherwise DP is the wrong tool"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Naive fib",
                "DP fib"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Recurrence",
                  "`fib(n-1) + fib(n-2)`",
                  "same recurrence"
                ],
                [
                  "Time",
                  "{red:O(2^n)}",
                  "{green:O(n)}"
                ],
                [
                  "Why",
                  "same subproblems recomputed",
                  "each state solved once"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. The DP Recipe",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "State",
                    "sub": "what dp[i] means",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Recurrence",
                    "sub": "from smaller states",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Base cases",
                    "sub": "smallest states",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Order",
                    "sub": "deps first",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Answer",
                    "sub": "read off dp",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Recompute the same state twice? ==Cache it==. Define the **state** first; the recurrence follows from it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Memoization vs Tabulation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Memoization vs Tabulation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Ways to Fill the Table",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Memoization} = top-down: recursion + cache keyed by state (`dict` or `@lru_cache`)",
                "{green:Tabulation} = bottom-up: fill a table in a loop from the base cases",
                "Same time for both: ==states × work per transition=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Memoization",
                "Tabulation"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Computes",
                  "only **reached** states",
                  "every state"
                ],
                [
                  "Stack",
                  "{red:recursion depth risk}",
                  "{green:none}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@lru_cache(None)",
                "def fib(n):",
                "    if n < 2: return n",
                "    return fib(n-1) + fib(n-2)"
              ],
              "note": "memo: cache key is n"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Save Space and Choose",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Rolling array==: keep only what the next step reads",
                "fib needs **two variables**; a 2D table reading the previous row needs **one row**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "a, b = 0, 1",
                "for _ in range(n):",
                "    a, b = b, a + b"
              ],
              "note": "tabulation, O(1) space: a is fib(n)"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pick memo: {blue:few states reachable} or awkward order",
                "Pick tabulation: {green:deep recursion} or space optimization matters"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mutable cache key",
              "text": "A `list` argument is unhashable, so the cache fails. Pass a ==tuple== or an **index** instead."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
