              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. LCS",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "State: `dp[i][j]` = ==LCS length== of first `i` chars of a, first `j` of b",
                "Match: `dp[i-1][j-1] + 1`",
                "No match: `max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1])`",
                "Time and space {green:O(mn)}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Subsequence",
                "Substring"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Order kept",
                  "yes",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "May skip chars",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{red:no}"
                ],
                [
                  "`ace` in `abcde`",
                  "yes",
                  "no"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. LIS",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "O(n²): `dp[i] = 1 + max(dp[j])` over `j<i` with `a[j]<a[i]`",
                "Answer is ==max(dp)==, not `dp[n-1]`",
                "O(n log n): keep a ==tails== array, find the slot with `bisect_left`",
                "`bisect_right` allows equal values (non-decreasing)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from bisect import bisect_left",
                "tails = []",
                "for x in [5, 6, 1]:",
                "    i = bisect_left(tails, x)",
                "    tails[i:i+1] = [x]",
                "print(len(tails), tails)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "2 [1, 6]"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "tails is not the LIS",
              "text": "Its **length** is the answer, but `[1, 6]` is not a subsequence of the input."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why is LIS max(dp)?** The best sequence can end at any index.",
                "**Subsequence vs substring?** Subsequence may skip characters; substring is contiguous.",
                "**Why bisect_left?** Equal values replace a tail, so the result stays strictly increasing."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
